          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தீப்பிடி — tīppiṭi — \"to catch fire\"."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "ஒருவேளை வீடு தீப்பிடித்தால், நாங்கள் உடனே வெளியே ஓடுவோம். oruvēḷai vīṭu tīppiṭittāl, nāṅkaḷ uṭaṉē veḷiyē ōṭuvōm. If the house were to catch fire, we would run out at once."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "Past (it …): தீப்பிடித்தது, tīppiṭittatu."
            },
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "The thing on fire is the subject; also written as two words, தீப் பிடி."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "type": "etymology",
          "title": "The word, taken apart",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "தீப்பிடி (tīppiṭi) is a Tamil compound built from தீ, \"fire\" (DEDR 3266), and பிடி, \"to catch, seize\" (DEDR 4148); the stop doubles after தீ."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "type": "notice",
          "title": "What you've built",
          "segments": [
            {
              "kind": "speech",
              "text": "One more word for telling what happened."
